  "decision": {
    "id": "VOICEUP-MEETING-X86-ARTIFACT-SOURCES-2026-09-10",
    "reviewed_on": "2026-09-10",
    "inventory_sha256": "403862bbd150130d09566193560c011863d2ece858028ca2ab5a487c39b14ef6",
    "spec_path": "specs/speaker-identity/PRDs/002-long-recording-analysis/PRD.md",
    "review_scope": "Independent official metadata and actual wheel review for the explicit local x86_64 meeting extension. All 63 admitted base pins retained; 68 new packages have exact verified artifacts and satisfied native Python3.13 dependency closure. Two Lightning packages use the mandatory CVE-2026-58659 security fix with immutable upstream code verification. This admits the local build, not native ARM64, physical Mac, full security-gate or end-to-end meeting accuracy.",
    "compatibility_evidence": [
      "docs/evidence/2026-09-08-local-speaker-pilot/package-releases.json: new backend packages released more than30 days ago",
      "docs/evidence/2026-09-08-local-speaker-pilot/inference-package-releases.json: runtime release dates",
      "Docker verified pgvector immutable index includes PostgreSQL17.11 and available vector0.8.6; extensionactivation remains reviewed migration",
      "Inference25 unit tests and fixed-hash model packaging passed; genuineCUDA test pending",
      "Backend immutable-image installation verified CPython3.13, soundfile0.14.0 and libsndfile1.2.2; runtime role has DML only and no schema CREATE.",
      "Final full application gate passed59backendtests (44unit,15realPostgreSQL) and21frontendtests; finalcontractregressionreport and JUnit are in docs/evidence/2026-09-08-local-speaker-pilot/.",
      "Dockerfile.offline reuses the reviewed Python base digest and107uniqueartifactcoordinates. Its62hash-verifiedwheel install passed with network disabled; this is now Compose default. See app/inference/evidence/offline-build.log and wheelhouse-verification.json.",
      "RealRTX4060CUDA/network-noneHTTPsmoke passed12checks; normalized192dimensionalECAPA on torch2.8.0+cu128; see app/inference/evidence/cuda-smoke.json. This is runtimecompatibility evidence, notspeakeraccuracy orbankadmission.",
      "docs/evidence/2026-09-09-spark-preflight/arm64-source-review.json: independent metadata closure and exact source review passed for48 artifacts,67active dependency edges;46exact artifacts and all9recent baseline pins retained. No version downgrade or fresh maturity exception.",
      "docs/evidence/2026-09-09-spark-preflight/python-base-platforms.json: same existing Python3.13.14 OCI index includes linux/arm64/v8; index bytes verified against its pinned digest.",
      "app/inference/requirements.spark.txt is deterministically generated from spark-wheelhouse-manifest.json by scripts/prepare-spark-wheelhouse.py. All 48 artifacts passed full size/hash verification on Spark; native networking-disabled installation and pip check passed. See docs/evidence/2026-09-09-spark-runtime/native-build.txt.",
      "docs/evidence/2026-09-09-spark-runtime/cuda-import-probe.json and cuda-smoke.json: real GB10 tensor and 9 HTTP checks passed with CUDA12.9/Torch2.8.0, VAD and normalized 192-dimensional ECAPA. Torch warns its compiled architecture list ends at SM120 while GB10 reports SM121; the observed tests passed, but do not establish all-kernel compatibility or speaker accuracy.",
      "64inference tests passed including28runtime-profile tests. Explicit architecture/Torch/CUDA guards preserve default x86_64-cu128 and opt-in aarch64-cu129; no CPU fallback. These tests use model doubles, not GPU hardware.",
      "docs/evidence/2026-09-10-local-cpu-runtime/cpu-artifact-source-review.json: independent official source and closure review, 60 unique artifacts, 47 artifacts and 65 active dependency edges per architecture; 45 common baseline versions retained.",
      "docs/evidence/2026-09-10-local-cpu-runtime/cpu-wheelhouse-verification.json: full artifact SHA256/size verification for both architectures; generated locks exactly reproduce their manifests.",
      "docs/evidence/2026-09-10-local-cpu-runtime/cpu-x86_64-http.json: genuine networking-disabled CPU ECAPA/Silero and nine HTTP smoke checks; constructed fixture establishes software compatibility, not speaker accuracy or Mac acceptance.",
      "CPU ARM64 OpenMP loader alias reuses the exact hash-verified library already inside the admitted Torch wheel; no new package or version. Final Dockerfile binding and independent source review record its SHA256. Runtime evidence is recorded separately.",
      "docs/evidence/2026-09-10-local-cpu-runtime/cpu-x86_64-final-http.json: final Dockerfile image passed nine real CPU HTTP checks with networking disabled.",
      "docs/evidence/2026-09-10-local-cpu-runtime/cpu-aarch64-native-verification.json and cpu-aarch64-native-http-smoke.json: the final ARM64 image passed nine real CPU HTTP checks on native Linux ARM64, without GPU access or network and with read-only filesystem, two CPUs and 4 GiB memory. Existing Spark services and model hashes were unchanged. This resolves model runtime compatibility beyond the separately recorded QEMU failure; it is not physical MacBook acceptance or a speaker accuracy benchmark.",
      "docs/evidence/2026-09-10-meeting-runtime/production-candidate-actual-wheel-audit.json: all68 actual artifacts verified; all63 base pins preserved; native Python3.13 target tags and dependency edges satisfied.",
      "docs/evidence/2026-09-10-meeting-runtime/proposed-meeting-closure-review.json: independent252 active constraints across131 distributions, zero conflicts.",
      "The exact extension installed with pip check passing in a network-disabled native Python3.13.14/Torch2.8.0+cu128 RTX4060 probe. Community1 processed the16-second public fixture. ASR execution and full application acceptance are recorded separately after model preparation.",
      "https://github.com/Lightning-AI/pytorch-lightning/releases/tag/2.6.6 documents both checkpoint code execution fixes. Actual wheel saving.py matches immutable upstream771017e4f39b314b49abd4a1d65905c74268d248 after package namespace normalization; remaining GHSA-qqmf-gpg7-g8gw metadata contradiction is explicitly triaged, not a passing release scanner."
    ],
